       {
        "texto": "Du er forelsket i Louise, …",
        "lengua": "estudio"
       },
       {
        "texto": "**ikke?**",
        "lengua": "estudio"
       }
      ],
      [
       {
        "texto": "Hun var **ikke** køn for to år siden, …",
        "lengua": "estudio"
       },
       {
        "texto": "**vel?**",
        "lengua": "estudio"
       }
      ]
     ],
     "nota": "Affirmative → **ikke?** · Sentence with a negation → **vel?** Much easier than English tags.",
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "da or når",
     "texto": [
      "- **da** = when, **a single time in the past**: Hun var irriterende, **da** hun var yngre.\n- **når** = when, **present, future or repeated**: **Når** vi holder fest i næste uge… · **Når** man mødte hende, var hun sur (every time).\n\nIn English it's just one word ('when'); in Danish you have to think: a single time in the past? → **da**."
     ],
     "tutora": "pensando"
    },
